---
import Layout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/wrapper/Section.astro";
import ContentWrapper from "@/components/wrapper/ContentWrapper.astro";
import Grid from "@/components/wrapper/Grid.astro";
import Heading from "@/components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Paragraph from "@/components/typography/Paragraph.astro";
import Eyebrow from "@/components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import Button from "@/components/Button.astro";
import ButtonWrapper from "@/components/wrapper/ButtonWrapper.astro";
import MembershipForm from "@/components/content/MembershipForm.astro";
import MembershipFees from "@/components/content/MembershipFees.astro";
import GrowingFoundation from "@/components/content/GrowingFoundation.astro";
import RichText from "@/components/typography/RichText.astro";
import Card from "@/components/item/Card.astro";
import Accordion from "@/components/interactive/Accordion.astro";
import AccordionItem from "@/components/interactive/AccordionItem.astro";
import {
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
  CONTACT_PHONE,
  CONTACT_PHONE_HREF,
  LETTER_PDF,
} from "@/consts";
---

<Layout
  title="Membership"
  description="Become a founding member of OPSA. Read Dr. Zameer Pirani’s letter to physician colleagues and register your interest."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <Section theme="dark">
    <ContentWrapper variant="columns">
      <Eyebrow>Founding membership</Eyebrow>
      <Heading tag="h1" class="heading-accent" maxWidth={22}>
        Help shape the future
        <br />
        <strong>of pain care.</strong>
      </Heading>
      <Paragraph variant="large" maxWidth={56}>
        Join Ontario’s pain specialists, patients and communities in building a
        shared voice for better care.
      </Paragraph>
      <ButtonWrapper>
        <Button element="link" href="#register" variant="directional">
          Become a founding member
        </Button>
        <Button element="link" href="#letter" emphasis="secondary">
          Read our letter to physicians
        </Button>
      </ButtonWrapper>
      <GrowingFoundation slot="column2" />
    </ContentWrapper>
  </Section>
  <!-- Letter -->
  <Section
    id="letter"
    aria-labelledby="letter-heading"
    containerClass="max-width-reading"
  >
    <ContentWrapper>
      <Eyebrow>A letter to our physician colleagues · November 8, 2026</Eyebrow>
      <Heading id="letter-heading" maxWidth={27}>
        An invitation to join OPSA as a founding member
      </Heading>
      <ButtonWrapper>
        <Button element="link" href={LETTER_PDF} download emphasis="secondary">
          Download the letter (PDF)
        </Button>
      </ButtonWrapper>
    </ContentWrapper>
    <RichText variant="main">
      <p>Dear Colleagues,</p>
      <p>
        I am writing to physicians and clinic leaders across Ontario who already
        provide image-guided pain care. Your practices show every day what safe,
        specialist-led care looks like. I am inviting you to join the Ontario
        Pain Specialist Association (OPSA), so that together we can make this
        standard the norm and create real distinction in chronic pain medicine
        in this province.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chronic pain is a leading cause of lost work, strained families and
        diminished quality of life, yet the care patients receive varies widely.
        You have likely seen the consequences: patients arriving after
        injections performed without image guidance, or by practitioners without
        recognized training in pain medicine. Meanwhile, the value of specialist
        pain care is not always recognized. Patients' experiences rarely inform
        policy, and the system lacks a connected approach. Strong
        community-based pain care, close to home, could also ease pressure on
        our emergency departments and hospitals.
      </p>
      <p>
        OPSA believes people living with pain can get better. We advocate for
        specialist-led, image-guided pain care as the standard for every
        Ontarian. That means:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Image guidance:</strong> interventional procedures performed
          under image guidance, for accuracy and safety.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Appropriate training:</strong> procedures performed by
          appropriately trained pain specialists.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Holistic care:</strong> interventions delivered as part of a
          comprehensive plan that includes medical management, rehabilitation
          and psychological support where needed.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Working with patients, caregivers, government stakeholders, and health
        system partners, we champion safe, evidence-based care. Our goal is
        simple: help people live their best lives with less pain, and return to
        work, family and community.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your voice carries weight with patients, policymakers and peers. I am
        asking you to stand with us in one or more of these ways:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Become a founding member.</strong> OPSA is being incorporated
          as a membership-funded, not-for-profit corporation under Ontario's{" "}
          <em>Not-for-Profit Corporations Act, 2010</em>. Founding members will
          shape its direction from day one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>
            Sign on as a supporting clinic, endorsing our position
          </strong>{" "}
          that specialist-led, image-guided care should be the standard of care
          in Ontario.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Take on a leadership role.</strong> We are building our board
          and leads for clinical advocacy, education, membership and community
          engagement.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Spread the word</strong> among colleagues, residents, fellows
          and partner specialties, including primary care, who share these
          values.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        <strong>A founding financial commitment.</strong> OPSA will be funded by
        its members, not by industry. To launch our work, I am asking each
        founding member to pay a one-time{" "}
        <strong>initiation fee of $400</strong>, which covers the first month,
        followed by a <strong>monthly fee on a sliding scale</strong> based on
        the number of members. Based on 25 founding physicians, the monthly fee
        is about $290 (see the <a href="#membership-fees">Appendix</a>). This
        will fund OPSA's early initiatives, including incorporation, advocacy
        with government and health system partners, and patient and physician
        education. Because the cost is shared, each member's contribution will
        decrease as our membership grows.
      </p>
      <p>
        Membership registration opens soon. In the meantime, please{" "}
        <a href="#register">register your interest</a> at opsa.pages.dev, or
        reply to me directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ontarians living with pain should not have to wonder whether the care
        they receive is safe or effective. With your support, OPSA can make
        specialist-led, image-guided care the expectation rather than the
        exception.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thank you for considering this invitation. I look forward to working
        with you.
      </p>
      <p>With warm regards,</p>
      <p>
        <strong>
          Dr. Zameer Pirani, MD, FRCPC (Anesthesia &amp; Pain Medicine)
        </strong>
        <br />
        Founder &amp; Chair Ontario Pain Specialist Association (OPSA)
        <br />
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
        <br />
        <a href={CONTACT_PHONE_HREF}>{CONTACT_PHONE}</a>
      </p>
    </RichText>
    <MembershipFees id="membership-fees" />
    <ButtonWrapper>
      <Button
        element="link"
        href="#register"
        variant="directional"
      >
        Become a founding member
      </Button>
      <Button element="link" href="#membership-questions" emphasis="secondary">
        Membership questions
      </Button>
    </ButtonWrapper>
  </Section>
  <!-- Membership options -->
  <Section class="background-2">
    <ContentWrapper>
      <Eyebrow>A shared purpose</Eyebrow>
      <Heading>There’s a place for you in OPSA</Heading>
      <Paragraph maxWidth={62}>
        Pain care is shaped by many perspectives. Register your interest and let
        us know how you would like to be involved.
      </Paragraph>
    </ContentWrapper>
    <Grid large={3}>
      <Card
        variant="feature"
        symbol="evidence"
        heading="Physicians and clinic leaders"
        text="Help shape clinical advocacy, education and a shared standard for specialist-led, image-guided care."
      />
      <Card
        variant="feature"
        symbol="people"
        heading="Patients and caregivers"
        text="Bring lived experience into conversations about pain care and what better care makes possible."
      />
      <Card
        variant="feature"
        symbol="connected"
        heading="Community and health system partners"
        text="Connect organizations and communities working toward better pain care across Ontario."
      />
    </Grid>
    <Card
      heading="Founding physician membership"
      text="$400 one-time initiation fee (covers the first month), then a sliding-scale monthly share of about $290 based on 25 founding physicians."
      buttonEmphasis="primary"
      buttonLabel="Read the letter to physicians"
      buttonHref="#letter"
    />
  </Section>
  <!-- Registration -->
  <Section id="register" theme="dark" aria-labelledby="register-heading">
    <ContentWrapper variant="sticky-content">
      <Eyebrow>Register your interest</Eyebrow>
      <Heading id="register-heading">
        Be part of the founding membership.
      </Heading>
      <Paragraph>
        Membership opens once OPSA completes incorporation. Everyone who
        registers interest will be contacted first.
      </Paragraph>
      <Paragraph>
        This form registers your interest; no payment is collected here.
      </Paragraph>
      <MembershipForm slot="column2" />
    </ContentWrapper>
  </Section>
  <!-- FAQ -->
  <Section id="membership-questions">
    <ContentWrapper variant="columns">
      <Eyebrow>Your questions</Eyebrow>
      <Heading>Membership, explained.</Heading>
      <Paragraph>
        Find answers about membership, shared funding and how to register your
        interest in OPSA.
      </Paragraph>
      <Accordion slot="column2">
        <AccordionItem heading="How is OPSA funded?" open>
          <Paragraph>
            OPSA is funded by its members, not by industry. Founding physician
            members pay a one-time $400 initiation fee, then a monthly share on
            a sliding scale that falls as membership grows (about $290 per month
            based on 25 founding physicians). Details are in our letter to
            physician colleagues on this page.
          </Paragraph>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem heading="When does membership open?">
          <Paragraph>
            Membership opens once OPSA completes incorporation. Everyone who
            registers interest will be contacted first.
          </Paragraph>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem heading="Who can register interest?">
          <Paragraph>
            Pain specialists, physicians, clinic leaders, patients, caregivers,
            patient advocates, and community and health system partners are
            invited to express their interest.
          </Paragraph>
        </AccordionItem>
      </Accordion>
    </ContentWrapper>
  </Section>
</Layout>
